---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import graph from '../data/railway-graph.json';

const stationCount = graph.metadata.totalStations.toLocaleString('en-IN');

const title = 'About RailKM — Indian Railway Distance & Multi-Via Route Engine';
const description = `RailKM is a free track-distance and multi-via route engine for Indian Railways, computing the shortest rail kilometres between any two of ${stationCount} indexed stations with full intermediate halt lists.`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} backHref="/" backLabel="Back to Route Mapper">
	<div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 pb-24 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
		<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="data-mono text-eyebrow uppercase text-muted">
			<ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
				<li><a class="focus-ring rounded-sm transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/">Home</a></li>
				<li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
				<li class="text-foreground">About</li>
			</ol>
		</nav>

		<p class="mt-8 data-mono text-eyebrow font-medium uppercase text-muted">About RailKM</p>
		<h1 class="mt-5 text-balance text-heading-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
			Exact track distance for every Indian Railways journey
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-muted">
			RailKM is a free, fast distance and multi-via route engine for Indian Railways. It computes
			the shortest track kilometres between any two of {stationCount} indexed stations, chains up
			to eight stops into a single break-journey plan, and lists every intermediate halt with its
			cumulative distance.
		</p>

		<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8">
			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">What RailKM does</h2>
				<ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md text-muted">
					<li>Computes the shortest track distance between any origin and destination.</li>
					<li>Chains multi-via journeys (up to eight stops) for break-journey routing.</li>
					<li>Lists every intermediate station with cumulative kilometres.</li>
					<li>Flags double-backs where the route revisits a station.</li>
					<li>Resolves legacy ⇄ modern station codes such as JHS ⇄ VGLJ and CSTM ⇄ CSMT.</li>
					<li>Estimates standard-class fares and exports a print / PDF route card.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">How the distance engine works</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					The network is modelled as a weighted graph of {stationCount} stations connected by
					18,994 track segments. RailKM runs a binary-heap Dijkstra search that minimises total
					track kilometres, then walks the resolved path to produce a leg-by-leg breakdown with
					cumulative distance at every halt. Every result is computed on the fly, in the browser,
					from a single pre-rendered graph file.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Where the data comes from</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					Distances are derived from open Indian Railways timetable data published by
					<a class="focus-ring rounded-sm text-link transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="https://datameet.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">DataMeet</a>. Per-segment
					kilometres are reconstructed from train timetables and validated against known route
					distances. RailKM is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
					operated by Indian Railways or IRCTC.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Accuracy &amp; limitations</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM reports the shortest <em>track</em> route by total kilometres — not the fastest
					or the most frequently served train path. Figures are indicative and may differ slightly
					from published timetables due to data availability. For ticketing, timings and official
					fares, always confirm with Indian Railways or IRCTC.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">What RailKM is not</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM does not sell tickets and does not provide live running status. It is a planning
					and reference tool for distances, intermediate stations, break-journey feasibility and
					approximate fares.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Start mapping</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					Open the mapper to plan a route, or browse the pre-computed directory of popular
					railway distance routes.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
					<a
						href="/"
						class="focus-ring inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center gap-2 rounded-sm border border-foreground bg-foreground px-4 py-2.5 text-label-sm font-medium text-background transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
					>
						Open the route mapper <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
					</a>
					<a
						href="/#popular-routes"
						class="focus-ring inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center gap-2 rounded-sm border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-2.5 text-label-sm text-foreground transition-colors hover:border-foreground/40"
					>
						Browse popular routes
					</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
